D3 Movie Genre Trends Over Time Description of Visualization: This visualization performs a medium-level task - comparing movie genre trends over time (1990-2017). The marks are lines showing each genre's trajectory, filled areas beneath the lines, and circles that appear on hover. The channels are x-position for year, y-position for movie count, and color for genre type (e.g., green for Drama, blue for Comedy). The design uses layered elements: semi-transparent areas in the background and solid lines in the foreground, with a vertical tracking line and tooltip appearing on mouse hover to show exact values. Users can click legend items to show/hide genres, zoom to specific time periods using buttons, and watch an initial animation that draws the lines from left to right. The visualization follows standard practices like using consistent colors throughout, adding grid lines for reference, and applying smooth curves to make trends easier to follow. This multi-line chart design allows simultaneous comparison of all ten genres' popularity patterns over the 27-year period.

